## What if I could start anywhere on the page?

The thing I keep coming back to is a sheet of paper. I can write the names of a few pubs down one side. If Tim asks where the first one is, I can sketch the station in the space beside it and draw the walk from there. Nothing about writing the first name commits the rest of the sheet to being a list.

I wonder what the equivalent on a computer would feel like. Imagine I can click anywhere on a blank page and start typing, speak, or insert something I already have. I click near the top and type “Five pubs near the station”. Halfway through, I realize I’d quite like someone to find them for me. I finish the line, select it and send it to an agent. I could just as easily have pressed Return and carried on writing my own list under that heading.

Suppose a map comes back. Looking at the pins, I can see that four places are close together and one is a fair way out. I select the four and ask aloud, “Could we walk between these?” Now the agent has somewhere specific to look. When the route appears, I click beneath it and type “Meet outside the station at six.” That line is for Tim. I’d like to be able to leave it there without the computer answering me.

Seeing the route gives me a better idea of what I want to send Tim. “Make this a flyer for Saturday. Keep the map, but give us somewhere to say where we’re meeting.” Once I see the flyer, I can tell the meeting time is too easy to miss. I select it and make the type bigger.

I’m used to building something like that from the pieces up. Find the addresses, plot the stops, fit the map around the copy. By the time I’ve polished it enough to see the whole thing, changing my mind feels expensive. One thing I like about working with AI is how cheaply I can get a whole first draft in front of me and take it apart again. Sometimes I need to see the thing I asked for before I can tell what I actually want.

If Tim says we should skip the last pub, I’d like him to be able to move the finish on the map himself. A flyer that looks lovely but makes us start over to change the route would lose much of what I liked about the blank page. I get to decide what I’m making partway through making it.

